  "identification_contract": {
    "checked_on": "2026-08-27",
    "reason": "Retail antennas do not reliably carry a user-readable Leshy2 role, and connector mechanics alone cannot distinguish several safe and unsafe same-family combinations.",
    "device_side": "Every outward port carries a short kit code plus its role and band in unobscured outer-face silkscreen. A post-PCBA colour collar around the connector base repeats the code colour; coloured PCB silkscreen is not assumed.",
    "antenna_side": "Every kit antenna receives a durable printed heat-shrink flag at its connector end with the same kit code, role and band. The package slot repeats the same data.",
    "accessibility": "Text and code are authoritative and remain sufficient for colour-vision deficiency; colour is redundant only.",
    "nrf24_rule": "N1, N2 and N3 antennas are electrically interchangeable, but individual codes preserve a one-glance installed-kit inventory.",
    "substitution_rule": "A substitute antenna receives the code of the qualified profile, never a code inferred only from connector type or appearance.",
    "fpv_r2_result": "TBS5G8MMCXA is the exact linear first target for the FPV RX 5.8G MMCX port; its printed FPV code and band are repeated on the antenna flag and package slot.",
    "fpv_r2_gate": "A supply-independent fallback and assembled sensitivity/mechanical HIL remain open before antenna-kit freeze."
  },
